 },
 "findings": [
  "Measured on the nine names' own daily prices from 2017-01-04 to 2026-11-12, the book at 1.00x runs 29% volatility, a one-month 95% expected shortfall of 18.9% (the most cautious of historical 14.9%, filtered 16.3% and Student-t 18.9%) and a one-year 95% drawdown of 44%, against limits of 12%, 20% and 25%.",
  "The limits allow 0.63x (shortfall), 0.68x (volatility) and 0.53x (drawdown); the drawdown cap binds, so the book's size is 0.53x. Keeping every name at full size instead takes a Nasdaq-100 futures short of 82% of NAV.",
  "Exposures: Nasdaq-100 beta 1.14 (broad market 1.54 now, 1.34 over ten years), semis net of the market -0.32, rates -0.17. 82% of the variance is the market and 16% is stock-specific: effective independent bets 1.6 of nine.",
  "Hedges walked forward from 2017-07-06: a Nasdaq-100 short at the measured beta cut the variance 90% and turned 2022 from -42% to -0.2%; the long bond held only when its correlation said it hedged cut it 3% (2022 -45%), and a standing 30% long bond 0% (2022 -48%).",
  "Stock-bond correlation (63-day, book against the 20-year bond): +0.00, state neutral. On the book's worst 5% of days since 2022 the bond rose 55% of the time.",
  "The one-day 99% VaR, backtested on the book: a normal model at today's volatility was breached 55 times against 24 expected (p 0.000); filtered historical simulation 15 against 22 (p 0.13)."
 ],
